src/boonza/matchmaker.py and secondary.chimerax_ss port UCSF ChimeraX code:
the Needleman-Wunsch alignment (alignment_algs/_nw/nw.cpp, support.cpp) and
the Kabsch-Sander secondary-structure assignment (atomstruct CompSS.cpp),
Copyright 2022 Regents of the University of California, which ChimeraX
distributes under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1; the two
files carry ChimeraX's notice and are distributed under that license.  The
default parameters, pairing and pruning rules follow ChimeraX matchmaker
(match_maker, std_commands/align.py), which is covered by the ChimeraX
license (https://www.rbvi.ucsf.edu/chimerax/docs/licensing.html).  The
BLOSUM-62 matrix is from the BLOCKS database (Henikoff & Henikoff, 1992).

boonza's solvate, neutralize and hydrogen mass repartitioning (boonza/build.py)
follow msys's dms-solvate, dms-neutralize and dms-hmr tools, and
boonza/data/tip3p.dms is the TIP3P water box distributed with msys, under the
msys license above.

