src/boonza/data/fragments holds two fragment libraries for boonza swim, as
SDF files of structures and their properties:

  AstexMiniFrag.sdf   63 fragments, the MiniFrag approach of Astex
                      Pharmaceuticals (O'Reilly et al., "Crystallographic
                      screening using ultra-low-molecular-weight ligands
                      (MiniFrags)", Drug Discovery Today 24 (2019) 1081)
  Essential320.sdf    307 fragments, from the Essential Fragment Library

Both files came from Enamine's fragment libraries
(https://enamine.net/compound-libraries/fragment-libraries) and keep its
catalogue identifiers (Z359510198, ...); each is a subset of the set
published there.  Enamine states no licence with the files themselves; its
site terms (https://enamine.net/terms-of-use) restrict redistributing
catalogue content.  The structures themselves come from the published
fragment sets cited above.
